# The browser app's configuration, which is deliberately almost empty.
#
# Copy to `.env` only if you need to override something. Nothing here is required: the app builds
# and runs with this file absent, which is how it is deployed.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed `VITE_` to the browser. Treat everything in this file as
# public — it is compiled into the JavaScript bundle and anyone can read it. Secrets belong in
# `api/.env`, which the server reads and never sends anywhere.

# Where the API lives. LEAVE THIS UNSET unless you know you want the trade-off below.
#
# Unset means every call is a relative `/api/...`, so the API is same-origin with the page. That
# is what lets the login cookie stay `SameSite=Lax`. It resolves correctly in all three places
# this app runs, without being configured in any of them:
#
#   local dev  — `vite.config.js` proxies /api to http://127.0.0.1:8000
#   Render     — the API process serves this app itself, so /api is genuinely the same server
#   Vercel     — `vercel.json` rewrites /api/* to the Render service, so the browser still sees
#                one origin even though the API is on another host
#
# Setting it points the app at an API on a different origin. That makes the session cookie a
# third-party cookie, which Safari and Brave block by default and Firefox partitions — users on
# those browsers would be unable to log in at all. `docs/decisions.md` records why we route
# through the Vercel rewrite instead.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-service.onrender.com
